cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "EnerGIS: Modular MILP Framework for Industrial Heat Network Planning"
message: >-
  If you use this software in your research, please cite it using
  the metadata from this file.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ruess
    given-names: Lukas
repository-code: "https://github.com/LukasRuess98/Planing-Framework-for-Heat"
license: MIT
version: "2.0.0-alpha"
date-released: "2026-03-25"
keywords:
  - district heating
  - MILP
  - energy system optimization
  - rolling horizon
  - Pyomo
  - heat pump
  - thermal storage
abstract: >-
  EnerGIS is a modular mixed-integer linear programming (MILP) framework
  for planning and optimizing industrial district heating networks.
  It supports heat pumps, thermal storage, thermal generators, and
  network loss modeling with rolling horizon and model predictive
  control workflows.
